  "classification": "Level-3 bounded access-path diagnostics on recent writes; physical cache residency unverified",
  "same_bytes_per_pair": true,
  "limits": [
    "FUSE performs staging/file fsync/rename/directory fsync; HTTP uses a size-checked PUT receipt with fsync=true. Publication semantics differ.",
    "Native HTTP payloads pass through the filer; FUSE uses metadata RPCs and direct volume I/O. This is a complete access-path comparison, not an isolated FUSE-overhead measurement.",
    "Both FUSE mounts remain running during all trials; idle watch/cache costs are common co-tenancy.",
    "Only 256 operations per cell; p99 is a small-sample observation and p99.9 unavailable.",
    "Rates exclude generation, external-witness fsync, connection setup and orchestration. Recent writes with no explicit cache eviction; physical cache residency is unverified. Fresh processes do not establish physical cold-read performance.",
    "Native cgroup deltas include all trials, exact readback and background work in the snapshot window. They are not per-path costs.",
    "Compression/codec comparison unrun: high-entropy bodies, no enabled workload codec; allocated/logical ratios include RF3, metadata, volume and cache allocation.",
    "Timed trials verify exact bodies after each write phase and at the end; no concurrent periodic readback runs inside the timed write loops. The live writer/reader fault test is separate.",
    "No physical power-loss or independent-host durability claim. Process loss is distinct from permanent disk or metadata-quorum loss."
  ],
